  "purpose": "SA-002 pre-promotion traceability: every expected value of a vector proposed for normative status must trace to a normative clause, and its inputs must be consumable without the reference implementation.",
  "blockers": {
    "T-UNSIGNED": "Artifact has no alg, kid or signature and the options carry no trustedKeySets or mode. The expected verdict relies on a non-strict verification mode that no normative document defines (authorization-v1 \u00a79 defines strict mode only). Materialize as signed strict-mode artifacts before promotion. Applies to authorization-verification and clock-semantics-verification.",
    "T-NOT-MATERIALIZED": "The vector carries a mode name, not an artifact. The artifact is built at run time by packages/conformance/src/validate.ts, so an independent implementation cannot consume the vector without the TypeScript generator. Materialize artifacts and options, as the wire-encoding corpus does. Applies to authorization-signature-verification and key-lifecycle-verification.",
    "T-PROJECTION-UNSPECIFIED": "The expected hash is the PolicyEngine INTENT_BINDING_FIELDS projection (signature and _internal_trace_id excluded). external-provider-profile.md:119 names the projection but no normative document lists its fields; sha256(canonical(input)) does not match (checked). Issuer-side behavior, not verifier behavior. Applies to intent-hash."
  },
